    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d715-a1">

                <pb facs="0732" n="634" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg634"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">C. T. Wang</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <p rendition="#flush">L–137</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your formal note (No. 118, July 23, 1930)<anchor n="9" xml:id="d715-f1"/>
                    stating that Mr. Joseph W. Ballantine has been assigned as Consul General at
                    Canton, and requesting that the appropriate authorities be instructed to receive
                    him in accordance with precedent.</p>
                <p>I have not failed to note the above, and have submitted a request to the Chairman
                    of the National Government for the issuance of an exequatur for the above-named
                    Consul General in order to enable him to perform his duties.</p>
                <p>Aside from having notified by note the competent local authorities to receive him
                    in accordance with precedent, I have the honor, Mr. Minister, to enclose
                    herewith an exequatur for transmission.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d715-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wang Cheng-t’ing</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-14">August 14, 1930</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
